---
import AppLayout from '../../layouts/AppLayout.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import { getMessages, localePath } from '../../i18n';
import AgentToSeedBridge from '../../components/AgentToSeedBridge.astro';
import SeedOwnedComputePath from '../../components/SeedOwnedComputePath.astro';
import { openEvoScientificState } from '../../lib/openEvoScientificState';
const m = getMessages('en');
const guideRecord = (await getCollection('guides'))[0]?.data;
---
<AppLayout title={m.guide.pageTitle} description="Understand Agent, SEED, and OpenEvo runtime/training mechanisms, then enter traceable WebShop experiment state and reproduction guidance." locale="en">
  <div class="shell editorial-page guide-learning-page" data-guide-source={guideRecord ? 'collection' : 'fallback'}>
    <header class="page-header guide-primary" data-reader-primary>
      <h1>Agent, SEED, and OpenEvo</h1>
      <p class="lede">Start from multi-step agent runtime, understand SEED parameter learning and OpenEvo cross-task evolution, then enter the WebShop experiment’s historical evidence, dated default-branch snapshot, and live-state source.</p>
      <div class="guide-primary-actions"><a class="button button-primary" href="#agent-run">See how an agent run works ↓</a><a class="button button-secondary" href={localePath('en','/research/seed-openevo/study/results/')}>Go to WebShop findings</a></div>
    </header>

    <div id="agent-run"><AgentToSeedBridge locale="en" /></div>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="seed-guide-title">
      <div class="section-heading"><div><span class="section-kicker">Paper method</span><h2 id="seed-guide-title">SEED reproduction reference</h2></div></div>
      <p>The SEED paper uses Qwen2.5-3B-Instruct, ALFWorld, and WebShop, with hindsight-skill SFT, on-policy rollout, GRPO, and OPD. Strict reproduction should pin the paper model, task protocol, and training definition first.</p>
      <div class="guide-cards">
        <a href={localePath('en','/papers/seed/')}><strong>SEED paper</strong><span>Paper conditions, model roles, training stages, and reproduction material</span></a>
        <a href={localePath('en','/research/seed-openevo/flow/seed/')}><strong>SEED method</strong><span>Hindsight skills, OPD, GRPO, and parameter updates</span></a>
        <a href={localePath('en','/research/seed-openevo/flow/benchmarks/')}><strong>ALFWorld / WebShop</strong><span>Tasks, actions, scoring, and failure evidence</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <SeedOwnedComputePath locale="en" />

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="openevo-guide-title">
      <div class="section-heading"><div><span class="section-kicker">Experiment state</span><h2 id="openevo-guide-title">OpenEvo × WebShop</h2></div></div>
      <p>Formal experiments are maintained in <code>openevo-experiment</code>. When this site checked default <code>main</code> on <time datetime={openEvoScientificState.checkedAt}>{openEvoScientificState.checkedAt}</time>, <code>current-campaign.json</code> recorded <strong>{openEvoScientificState.defaultBranchSnapshot.phase}</strong> / <code>{openEvoScientificState.defaultBranchSnapshot.status}</code>. This is a dated default-branch snapshot, not a claim about any newer active scientific branch.</p>
      <p class="hardware-truth">Hardware tiers in the model catalog are coarse categories; the workspace VRAM calculator is a <strong>heuristic planning estimate</strong>, <strong>not a measured hardware result</strong>. {openEvoScientificState.gpuRule.en}</p>
      <p>{openEvoScientificState.liveStateRule.en}</p>
      <div class="guide-cards">
        <a href={localePath('en','/research/seed-openevo/study/run/')}><strong>Reproduction guide</strong><span>Runtime topology, experiment identity, WebShop contract, and state resolution</span></a>
        <a href={localePath('en','/research/seed-openevo/study/')}><strong>Experiment entry</strong><span>WebShop data flow, historical milestones, and live-state source</span></a>
        <a href={localePath('en','/research/seed-openevo/study/results/')}><strong>Experiment results</strong><span>Phase D–G historical evidence, default-branch snapshot, and live claim routing</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="history-guide-title">
      <div class="section-heading"><div><span class="section-kicker">History</span><h2 id="history-guide-title">RTX6 and retired repositories</h2></div></div>
      <p><code>seed3090</code> and <code>openevo-webshop</code> remain provenance sources for RTX6 (4×RTX3090) engineering, WebShop bring-up, failure traces, and early SD-LoRA diagnostics, but they are no longer current experiment entry points.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</AppLayout>

<style>
  .guide-cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.65rem}.guide-cards a{padding:1rem;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;color:inherit;text-decoration:none}.guide-cards strong,.guide-cards span{display:block}.guide-cards span{margin-top:.4rem;color:var(--muted);font-size:.76rem;line-height:1.45}.section>p{max-width:78ch;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.65}.hardware-truth{padding:.75rem .85rem;border-left:2px solid var(--accent-deep);background:var(--surface-muted);font-size:.78rem}@media(max-width:720px){.guide-cards{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
  .guide-primary{box-sizing:border-box;max-width:860px;min-height:calc(100svh - 110px);display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center;padding-block:clamp(2rem,6vh,3.5rem)}.guide-primary .lede{max-width:58ch}.guide-primary-actions{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.6rem;margin-top:1.1rem}@media(max-width:720px){.guide-primary{min-height:calc(100svh - 96px)}}
</style>